lines=['# Nigeria library expansion research','', '**Result: six institutions returned books for specific title queries. The requested ten verified institutions were not reached.** Ten major priorities are listed separately; four of those ten passed live query verification. The two additional successes (KASU and NIALS) are valuable candidates, but their national collection-size rank is not established.','', 'Checks ran on **15 November2026 UTC**; the parent research directory retains14November as its task date. All successes below came from direct HTTP responses saved in `evidence/`, not indexed snippets. No app adapter was run and no integration permission was obtained.','', '## Market and highest-value unlock','', 'Start with **Koha and NOUN**. A2025 published survey reports Koha at21of40responding federal-university libraries (52.5%, target43). This is evidence of concentration in that segment, not a national market-share estimate. Its table mixes repositories with ILS and its individual installations need current verification; for example, this investigation sees NewGenLib at Lagos and Benin. [Study and methods](https://acadrespub.com/index.php/oijlis/article/view/83).','', 'NOUN has one functioning integrated catalog with **42named branch/unit choices** covering study centres and faculty/central units. Those are candidate holdings locations, not42separately verified libraries or42deployments. A targeted search returned a headquarters record with two available copies. Reusing the Koha family potentially gives the best first deployment-to-location ratio; confirm actual coverage branch by branch. [Live catalog](https://koha.nou.edu.ng/).','', 'The National Library offers the largest documented public-service opportunity: approximately **5.2milliontitles/13.9millionvolumes and presence in33states plusFCT**, reported20August2024. None of these counts proves OPAC index coverage. Its robots policy disallows automated search and detail paths, so it is an institutional-partnership candidate rather than a verified connector. [Official collection/network statement](https://www.nln.gov.ng/news-details.php?post_Id=97&title=National+Library+Engages+Stakeholders+in+Southwest).','', 'Other significant networks include ABU’s main/academic/research complex (about10libraries in its2023/24handbook), and Babcock’s main library plus10branches. Babcock advertises90,477+volumes and external/community membership, but its catalog disallows all wildcard crawlers; no query was sent. Branch counts, buildings, and independent catalog deployments must remain separate. [Babcock official service/eligibility page](https://www.babcock.edu.ng/library).','', 'Nigeria is feasible as a **partner-led university rollout**, with a weaker currently verified public-library pathway. Six book-query successes show concrete technical opportunity. Many other major catalogs either declare automation restrictions, require authentication, or did not answer these probes. This does not establish nationwide outages or lack of infrastructure. Discoverability alone also does not make an academic library’s books borrowable by every app user.','', '## Ten major priorities, not an asserted national top ten','', 'No comparable recent national ranking was found. Counts mix books, volumes and journals, and come from different years. This is a deliberately major-collection/network shortlist, with dates and scope exposed. NOUN is selected for network reach instead of an unverified size total.','', '|Institution|Scale evidence (source date)|Platform|Live result|','|---|---|---|---|']
