lines+=['','## Failures, exclusions and follow-up','', 'The detailed machine-readable probe inventory is in `findings.json`; per-probe JSON records preserve request time, URL, status/error and snapshot path. Major unsuccessful candidates remain in the ten-priority table; additional checks included Jos, Central Bank, Abuja, Babcock, Covenant, LAUTECH, FUNAAB, Ilorin, Port Harcourt, Calabar, FUTMinna/FUTO/FUTA, LASU/Uyo/Bayero, and further universities.','', '- **Automation restriction:** National Library, Jos, Nile, Redeemer’s, Bowen, Adeleke, Babcock and Covenant. Covenant uses Primo/COLRIS; its robots disallows `/discovery/search` and `/primaws`. These search restrictions were not bypassed.','- **Auth boundary:** Ilorin’s OPAC returned401; no credentials or alternate access bypass attempted.','- **No returned books:** Abuja’s two publicly indexed Koha hosts returned real zero-result pages for broad searches; its main OPAC also returned zero for a known indexed title. University of Africa Toru-Orua returned zero for economics and the homepage-listed title Pragmatics. Neither is counted as a success, and neither result proves that the collection contains no books.','- **Current official endpoints that failed here:** Port Harcourt links `http://delopac.uniport.edu.ng`; Calabar’s libraryLinktree points to `http://38.17.48.240:8080/newgenlibctxt/`; FUTMinna’s resources page links `http://opac.futminna.edu.ng:8054/`. Each timed out. LASU’s official eLibrary redirected to a suspended-host page.','- **503/timeouts from this environment:** ABU, UNN, FUNAAB, Central Bank, AUN, LAUTECH and others. Secondary web-tool exact-title retrievals were also unavailable for ABU, CBN, ABUAD, KWASU and LAUTECH. Origin-versus-egress fault was not established; no general outage claim is made.','- **Final large-university checks:** Bayero has a current official homepage but its displayed search field has no submitted parameter or search action/handler. UNIZIK’s official footer links `https://opac.unizik.edu.ng:83`; this endpoint was tested separately. Modibbo Adama’s official library page describes credentialed terminals and off-campus databases, but no public physical-catalog search was identified. Usmanu Danfodiyo’s repository labels a homepage self-link OPAC; its linked eLibrary was investigated separately. These are not counted as book-query successes.','- **Important metadata limitation:** Benin’s public statistics show25,085booktitles/33,085copies, far below the handbook’s institution-wide267,501+bookvolumes. Its tested record includes imported MARC holdings labels from other institutions; these must not be interpreted as local copy availability. Lagos and Benin both return empty public availability summaries for the tested records.','', '## Engineering recommendation','', 'Pilot NOUN first, then evaluate OAU, KASU and NIALS using the existing Koha family with real adapter tests and explicit terms/permission review. OAU’s successful request took14.39s, while its detail timed out; performance must be tested against the app’s deadline. NewGenLib requires a new family for Lagos/Benin, including the public holdings AJAX semantics and edition identity preservation. The official Lagos endpoint is HTTP, which needs explicit handling; never silently disableTLSverification.','', 'The shortfall is **four more verified institutions**, plus collection-rank evidence. The highest-impact next work is agreements or institution-assisted tests for the major restricted/unreachable catalogs, followed by additional eligible large institutions. This report does not claim permission, production readiness, nationwide catalog coverage, or10verified institutions.','', '## Evidence and reproducibility','', '`probe.py`, `expand*.py`, `final_probes.py` and `save_sources.py` document the bounded direct-request approach. Saved evidence is capped at1.5MBper response. `build_report.py` generates this report and `findings.json` from those preserved responses and source notes. Re-running probes contacts external sites and must respect their then-current policies; the output alone is sufficient for offline parser replay.','']
(ROOT/'report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
